# What of Benchmark/ is published, and why.
#
# The directory is roughly 2.3 GB across ~38,000 files. Almost all of that is
# regenerable output: predicted structures, relaxed PDBs, cleaned scaffolds,
# per-cell logs. What goes in git is the code that produces it, the
# configuration that parameterises it, the task files that record exactly what
# was submitted, the CSVs every figure reads, and the figures and tables
# themselves. That is roughly 30 MB and it is enough to check any number in the
# manuscript without cluster access, and enough to regenerate the rest with it.
#
# Three of these rules exist to override the repo-root .gitignore, which ignores
# *.ipynb, *.fa and *.fasta globally. A nested .gitignore can re-include a file
# whose parent directory is not itself excluded, which is the case for both
# notebooks/ and designs/.

# ── Regenerable bulk ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cleaned scaffolds, CATH splits, LayerSelector caches, alt-weight shims (886 MB)
data/
# ESMFold and AF3 inputs and predicted structures (721 MB)
predictions/
# Relaxed PDBs from Phase 5 threading; also matched by the root's threaded*/
threaded/
# PyRosetta baseline working directories, one per cell (312 MB)
baselines/

# ── Logs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Slurm stdout, one file per array task
logs/slurm/
# Per-cell ProteinMPNN stdout. Kept out on the same reasoning as logs/slurm/:
# regenerable, and results/cells/*.json already carries the per-cell provenance
# independently. This closes the open item in logs/ISSUES.md that asked whether
# these should be published.
logs/mpnn/

# ── Per-record sidecars ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# results/*.csv is the published form of all of these. They are the inputs
# 10_aggregate.py reads, not the results, and there are ~2,700 of them.
results/cells/
results/threaded/
results/rejection/
# Per-cell sidecars from the superseded AvNAPSA nstruct 1 run, kept on disk
# as the evidence that s00 reproduces it (logs/ISSUES.md, 2026-08-26).
# Same class as results/cells/: an input to aggregation, not a result.
logs/nstruct1_backup/

# ── Editor and interpreter noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Re-included against the repo-root rules ────────────────────────────────────
# The analysis notebooks. Root ignores *.ipynb.
!notebooks/*.ipynb
# The designed sequences. One FASTA per cell, ~1.9 MB total, and the only place
# a reader can check a reported mutation set. Root ignores *.fa.
!designs/*.fa
